{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.65050459a1ce3ffe5cff6887.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"This proposal evaluates only the retained circular's classification routes for one Fund at a specified assessment time.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.65050459a1ce3ffe5cff6887.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The circular is applicable at that assessment time; the packet does not establish commencement.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.65050459a1ce3ffe5cff6887.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The threshold fact must be supplied using a supported exposure methodology, not inferred from illustrative holdings or disclosure language.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.65050459a1ce3ffe5cff6887.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"An operative SFC designation requires evidence of an actual designation; risk factors or the possibility of designation are insufficient.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.65050459a1ce3ffe5cff6887.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Unknown scope, exposure or designation facts remain unknown. Absence of designation evidence is not evidence of no designation.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"730c8c09c4ffcdfbe1727fdc284b30f37ab3bf850b9515d88730e5c73a3ec01e","candidate_id":"candidate.c99e8ea26b6c453a995574beb26ad6d3","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: whether the retained circular's complex-product classification trigger is satisfied for an in-scope Fund at the assessment time. True means aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure reaches at least 50% of NAV, or an operative SFC case-by-case designation exists, so the Fund must be treated as complex for distribution under this reading. False means both routes are affirmatively absent; it does not establish general non-complex status, compliance with sales duties or exemption under other instruments. An out-of-scope Fund receives no classification decision from this control. Missing evidence remains unresolved rather than producing false.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["modality"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The substantive distinction is automatic classification at the inclusive 50% threshold versus an actual discretionary SFC designation below it. Neither private-market exposure alone nor an adverse risk factor automatically establishes classification. LAF exclusion removes this circular's route without establishing that a LAF is non-complex under other rules. The text supports this single classification reading more strongly than competing automatic-classification rules; uncertainty chiefly concerns measurement, timing and missing evidence.","run_id":"run.daf6da18ef8f40588d4b69411abe2104","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"be86c12a28ac1c552b9cc386dfa44174629a63a786068d9bf5d8cdb44cbfa056","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Complex-product classification trigger for an SFC-authorised public Fund, excluding LAFs"}